---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';
import { FEE_DATA_VERSION, FEE_DATA_UPDATED } from '@/data/fees';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology & How We Verify Fees"
  description="How FeeCalc Tools sources, verifies, and updates payment processor and creator fee schedules — plus the public fee update checklist."
  canonicalPath="/methodology/"
>
  <h1>Methodology & how we verify fees</h1>
  <p class="answer-first">
    We store every fee schedule in one versioned data file with a source URL and last-verified date. Calculators use a
    transparent percent-plus-fixed formula with a documented reverse equation. Current data version:{' '}
    {FEE_DATA_VERSION} (updated {FEE_DATA_UPDATED}).
  </p>
  <h2>How calculations work</h2>
  <p>
    Forward: <code>fee = charge × percent + fixed</code>, <code>net = charge − fee</code>. Reverse:{' '}
    <code>charge = (desiredNet + fixed) ÷ (1 − percent)</code>, rounded to cents. Unit tests cover every schedule.
  </p>
  <h2>How we verify fees</h2>
  <p>
    Maintainers open each provider’s official pricing or fee policy page, update percent, fixed amount, currency, notes,
    source URL, and last-verified date in our dataset, then bump the public data version when material. After edits we
    run automated fee tests and a production build before publishing.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the official pricing URL for the schedule.</li>
    <li>Update percent, fixed, currency, notes, source URL, and last-verified date.</li>
    <li>Bump the fee data version and “last updated” date when the change is material.</li>
    <li>Run the full test suite and a static site build.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The maintainer checklist also lives in the repository at <code>docs/FEE-UPDATE.md</code>. Tool pages surface each
    schedule’s last-verified date next to the official source link.
  </p>
  <h2>Sourcing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Prefer the provider’s official pricing or fee policy page.</li>
    <li>Record currency, percent, fixed fee, and notes for regional caveats.</li>
    <li>When processing varies (Patreon, Ko-fi), label figures as blended estimates.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Update cadence</h2>
  <p>
    Fees change often. Material rate changes update <code>lastmod</code> and on-page “Last updated” dates. We prioritize
    corrections that include an official URL.
  </p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> with evidence. Include the tool
    URL, expected vs displayed fee, and a link to the official pricing page.
  </p>
  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>No payment brand sponsors our default rankings. Comparison sorts are by calculated fee for the selected amount.</p>
</BaseLayout>
